{"shortDescription":"Another heavyweight earnings week is ahead, with results from Big Tech, energy giants, chipmakers, financial services, healthcare, and industrial leaders set to offer a broad read on corporate spending, consumer resilience, and the outlook for market growth.Magnificent Seven members Microsoft NASDA…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Another heavyweight earnings week is ahead, with results from Big Tech, energy giants, chipmakers, financial services, healthcare, and industrial leaders set to offer a broad read on corporate spending, consumer resilience, and the outlook for market growth."]},{"type":"p","children":["Magnificent Seven members Microsoft ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:MSFT","text":"NASDAQ:MSFT"}},", Amazon ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:AMZN","text":"NASDAQ:AMZN"}},", and Alphabet ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:GOOGL","text":"NASDAQ:GOOGL"}}," headline the technology slate, alongside Intel ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:INTC","text":"NASDAQ:INTC"}},", KLA ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:KLAC","text":"NASDAQ:KLAC"}},", ServiceNow ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:NOW","text":"NYSE:NOW"}},", Fortinet ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:FTNT","text":"NASDAQ:FTNT"}},", and Vertiv ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:VRT","text":"NYSE:VRT"}},", as investors assess AI monetization, cloud demand, semiconductor spending, and data-center infrastructure. In energy, Exxon Mobil ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:XOM","text":"NYSE:XOM"}},", Chevron ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:CVX","text":"NYSE:CVX"}},", BP ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:BP","text":"NYSE:BP"}},", Phillips 66 ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:PSX","text":"NYSE:PSX"}},", Enterprise Products Partners ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:EPD","text":"NYSE:EPD"}},", ONEOK ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:OKE","text":"NYSE:OKE"}},", and Expand Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:EXE","text":"NASDAQ:EXE"}}," bring oil, gas, and refining trends into focus, while GE Vernova ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:GEV","text":"NYSE:GEV"}},", First Solar ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:FSLR","text":"NASDAQ:FSLR"}},", and Enphase Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:ENPH","text":"NASDAQ:ENPH"}}," offer a read on power generation and clean-energy demand."]},{"type":"p","children":["Financials and payments will also be in focus, with Visa ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:V","text":"NYSE:V"}},", Mastercard ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:MA","text":"NYSE:MA"}},", PayPal ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:PYPL","text":"NASDAQ:PYPL"}},", Coinbase ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:COIN","text":"NASDAQ:COIN"}},", Robinhood ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:HOOD","text":"NASDAQ:HOOD"}},", SoFi Technologies ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:SOFI","text":"NASDAQ:SOFI"}},", Strategy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:MSTR","text":"NASDAQ:MSTR"}},", and Ares Capital ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:ARCC","text":"NASDAQ:ARCC"}}," spanning consumer payments, digital assets, retail trading, and private credit. Healthcare names including Eli Lilly ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:LLY","text":"NYSE:LLY"}},", AbbVie ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:ABBV","text":"NYSE:ABBV"}},", Merck ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:MRK","text":"NYSE:MRK"}},", Bristol Myers Squibb ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:BMY","text":"NYSE:BMY"}},", Gilead Sciences ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:GILD","text":"NASDAQ:GILD"}},", Regeneron Pharmaceuticals ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:REGN","text":"NASDAQ:REGN"}},", GSK ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:GSK","text":"NYSE:GSK"}},", and Incyte ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:INCY","text":"NASDAQ:INCY"}}," will provide updates on drug demand and pharmaceutical pipelines. Meanwhile, Coca-Cola ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:KO","text":"NYSE:KO"}},", Starbucks ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:SBUX","text":"NASDAQ:SBUX"}},", Chipotle Mexican Grill ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:CMG","text":"NYSE:CMG"}},", Ford ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:F","text":"NYSE:F"}},", Boeing ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:BA","text":"NYSE:BA"}},", Caterpillar ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:CAT","text":"NYSE:CAT"}},", UPS ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:UPS","text":"NYSE:UPS"}},", and FedEx ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:FDX","text":"NYSE:FDX"}}," will shed light on consumer spending, manufacturing, and transportation activity."]},{"type":"p","children":["The broader lineup extends to uranium and copper miners, gold producers, cybersecurity firms, telecom infrastructure providers, data-center real estate companies, and high-growth consumer platforms such as Pinterest ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:PINS","text":"NYSE:PINS"}},", Roblox ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:RBLX","text":"NYSE:RBLX"}},", and Etsy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:ETSY","text":"NYSE:ETSY"}},". With such a wide cross-section of industries reporting, the week could offer important clues on where demand remains resilient, how AI investment is translating into business performance, and which sectors are navigating the most persistent cost and growth pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":["Below is a rundown of major quarterly updates anticipated in the week of October 26 to October 30:"]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Monday, October 26"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Verizon Communications ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:VZ","text":"NYSE:VZ"}}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Verizon Communications ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:VZ","text":"NYSE:VZ"}}," is set to report its Q3 2026 results before the market opens on Monday. The print is the first real test of CEO Dan Schulman's promise of positive phone net account growth after years of declines."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Q2, Verizon reported adjusted EPS of $1.30, beating consensus, while postpaid phone net additions reached 184,000. Revenue totaled approximately $34.3B, as equipment revenue fell 19.7% to $5.02B amid lower upgrade volumes and subsidy spending. Following the Frontier acquisition, fiber net additions rose to 155,000. Management raised its full-year adjusted EPS outlook for the second consecutive quarter to $4.99–$5.04 and expects 2026 postpaid phone net additions in the upper half of its 750,000–1 million target range."]},{"type":"p","children":["Recent developments have kept pricing and promotional activity in focus. Scotiabank lowered its price target to $50 from $51.50 while maintaining a Sector Outperform rating."]},{"type":"p","children":["Last week, Verizon also rolled out pre-orders for the latest iPhone lineup, including a switcher offer requiring no trade-in, highlighting the competitive promotions that could weigh on margins. Investors will look for progress on customer growth while assessing whether service revenue momentum and cost discipline can offset ongoing competitive pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":["Wall Street rates the stock a Buy, while Seeking Alpha's Quant rating holds a more cautious Hold."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Consensus EPS Estimate:"]}," $1.27"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Consensus Revenue Estimate:"]}," $34.85B"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Earnings Insight:"]}," Verizon has beaten EPS estimates in each of its last 8 quarters, surpassing revenue expectations in 50% of those reports."]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Also reporting"]},": Nucor ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:NUE","text":"NYSE:NUE"}},", Welltower ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:WELL","text":"NYSE:WELL"}},", Public Storage ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:PSA","text":"NYSE:PSA"}},", Cadence Design Systems ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:CDNS","text":"NASDAQ:CDNS"}},", Whirlpool ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:WHR","text":"NYSE:WHR"}},", Alliance Resource Partners ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:ARLP","text":"NASDAQ:ARLP"}},", Noble ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:NE","text":"NYSE:NE"}},", and more."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Tuesday, October 27"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["The Boeing Company ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:BA","text":"NYSE:BA"}}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Boeing ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:BA","text":"NYSE:BA"}}," is scheduled to report its Q3 2026 results before Tuesday’s open, with investors weighing progress toward 737 MAX certification milestones against persistent earnings and production challenges."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Q2, Boeing's revenue of $24.6B topped expectations, while its core loss of $0.76 per share was far wider than analysts had forecast. Commercial deliveries were 171 in Q2. In Q3, the company delivered 161 commercial aircraft, little changed from 160 a year earlier but below the prior quarter’s pace."]},{"type":"p","children":["Recent developments have offered some relief on labor and certification risks. Engineers represented by the SPEEA union ratified a new four-year contract, averting a potential strike that could have disrupted certification work on the 737 MAX 10 and 777X. However, a software glitch in the latest 737 MAX navigation update raised fresh concerns about certification delays. The FAA could approve the 737 MAX 10 in the near term, according to media reports, although the agency has emphasized that safety will determine the timeline. The smaller MAX 7 won approval in August. Investors will look for updates on certification, delivery momentum, and the company’s path toward more consistent financial performance."]},{"type":"p","children":["Wall Street rates the stock a Buy, while Seeking Alpha's Quant rating holds a more cautious Hold."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Consensus EPS Estimate:"]}," -$0.20"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Consensus Revenue Estimate:"]}," $24.37B"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Earnings Insight:"]}," Boeing has missed EPS consensus in 4 of its last 8 quarters, beating revenue estimates 6 times in that span."]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Also reporting"]},": PayPal Holdings ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:PYPL","text":"NASDAQ:PYPL"}},", Visa ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:V","text":"NYSE:V"}},", Expand Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:EXE","text":"NASDAQ:EXE"}},", The Coca-Cola Company ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:KO","text":"NYSE:KO"}},", Freeport-McMoRan ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:FCX","text":"NYSE:FCX"}},", W. P. Carey ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:WPC","text":"NYSE:WPC"}},", United Parcel Service ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:UPS","text":"NYSE:UPS"}},", SK Hynix ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:SKHY","text":"NASDAQ:SKHY"}},", SoFi ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:SOFI","text":"NASDAQ:SOFI"}},", Ares Capital ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:ARCC","text":"NASDAQ:ARCC"}},", American Tower ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:AMT","text":"NYSE:AMT"}},", Enphase Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:ENPH","text":"NASDAQ:ENPH"}},", Corning ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:GLW","text":"NYSE:GLW"}},",