"symbol":"NASDAQ:MSFT","text":"NASDAQ:MSFT"}}," is slated to report its fiscal Q1 2027 results after Wednesday's close, with investors looking for continued Azure growth vs. the roughly 45% guide, Copilot seat growth and monetization, commercial backlog, the capex trajectory, and the OpenAI-related impact on reported earnings."]},{"type":"p","children":["In fiscal Q4, revenue increased 18% Y/Y to $90.0B, while operating income rose 18% to $40.6B. Azure growth accelerated to 43%, with annual revenue surpassing $100B for the first time, while Microsoft Cloud revenue climbed 27% to $59.3B. Commercial remaining performance obligations reached $678B, up 84%, and Microsoft 365 Copilot surpassed 30 million paid seats. Results beat expectations, sending shares higher. For fiscal Q1, management guided revenue to $89.85B–$90.95B and Azure growth of approximately 45% in constant currency, while cautioning that capacity constraints remain."]},{"type":"p","children":["Recent analyst commentary has focused on Azure’s growth trajectory, Copilot adoption, and Microsoft’s relationship with OpenAI. Stifel upgraded the stock to Buy from Hold and raised its price target to $575, citing cloud and AI opportunities. Morgan Stanley has highlighted the durability of Azure growth and the potential impact of Microsoft’s OpenAI-related losses on reported earnings, noting that the losses are expected to reach a contractual cap by fiscal Q4. Investors will assess whether AI demand and infrastructure expansion can sustain growth while improving returns on investment."]},{"type":"p","children":["Wall Street rates the stock a Strong Buy, while Seeking Alpha's Quant rating holds a more cautious Hold."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Consensus EPS Estimate:"]}," $4.72"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Consensus Revenue Estimate:"]}," $90.72B"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Earnings Insight:"]}," Microsoft has beaten both EPS and revenue estimates in each of its last 8 quarters."]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Alphabet ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:GOOGL","text":"NASDAQ:GOOGL"}}," ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:GOOG","text":"NASDAQ:GOOG"}}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Alphabet ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:GOOGL","text":"NASDAQ:GOOGL"}}," is all set to report its Q3 2026 results after Wednesday's close with investors weighing rapid Google Cloud growth and expanding AI opportunities against rising capital expenditures and pressure on free cash flow."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Q2, revenue rose 24% Y/Y to $119.8B. Google Cloud revenue surged 82% to $24.8B, while operating income more than tripled to $8.8B, and its backlog reached $514B. Google Services revenue increased 15% to $94.5B, with Search revenue up 17% to $63.3B and YouTube advertising revenue rising 13% to $11.1B. GAAP EPS of $9.11 benefited from substantial gains on equity investments. However, capital expenditures reached $44.9B, leaving free cash flow negative at $5.9B, and management raised its full-year 2026 capex outlook to $195B–$205B"]},{"type":"p","children":["Recent developments have centered on Alphabet’s AI expansion. The company introduced Gemini 4 Argon and subsequently expanded its availability globally, with introductory API pricing set to increase after the initial promotional period. Analysts at Jefferies and BNP Paribas viewed the launch as supportive of Alphabet’s competitive position. In early October, Google launched a universal Gemini agent across Gmail, Drive, Docs, and Calendar to push deeper into enterprise AI, and TD Cowen raised its price target to $485 the same day."]},{"type":"p","children":["Wall Street rates the stock a Strong Buy, while Seeking Alpha's Quant rating holds a more cautious Hold."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Consensus EPS Estimate:"]}," $3.00"]},{"type":"*"